Given below are two statements:&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Assertion&nbsp;(A):</strong></td><td>A block near the surface of the earth, is pulled down by its weight&nbsp;<span class="math-tex">\((W);\)</span> the block, pulls the earth upward by exerting an equal force.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Reason&nbsp;(R):</strong></td><td>This is a consequence of Newton&#39;s law of action and reaction.</td></tr></tbody></table>
&nbsp;

<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td style="width: 6%;">1.</td><td>Both&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;are True and&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;is the correct explanation of&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td style="width: 6%;">2.</td><td>Both&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;are True but&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;is not the correct explanation of&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td style="width: 6%;">3.</td><td><strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;is True but&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;is False.</td></tr><tr><td style="width: 6%;">4.</td><td><strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;is False but&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;is True.</td></tr></tbody></table>
